  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Unnumbered location plan, PDA1-01, EXA1-01, Nosie Impact Assessment, Kitchen Extraction and Ventilation System Proposal and Risk Assessment for Odour- received 08/02/2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - Within 3 months of this decision, the details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall be carried out within 3 months and in accordance with the approval.",
    "Condition : 4 - The restaurant unit hereby approved shall not operate outside of the operating hours of 08:00 to 23:00 on Monday to Friday; 09:00 to 23:00 on Saturday; 10:00 to 22:00 on Sunday and on Public holidays without the prior written permission of the Local Planning Authority. This requirement shall be permanently adhered to.",
    "Condition : 5 - Delivery and collection times (including refuse collection) for the commercial premises hereby approved, shall only carried out between the following hours: Monday to Saturday between 07:00 and 22:00, Sunday between 09:00 to 20:00.",
    "Condition : 6 - Mechanical Services Noise Control: \r\na) The cumulative measured or calculated rating level of noise emitted from the mechanical services plant including heating, ventilation and air conditioning (HVAC) to which the application refers, shall be 10dB(A) below the existing background noise level, at all times that the mechanical system etc operates. The measured or calculated noise levels shall be determined at the boundary of the nearest ground floor noise sensitive premises or 1 meter from the facade of the nearest first floor (or higher) noise sensitive premises, and in accordance to the latest British Standard 4142; An alternative position for assessment /measurement may be used to allow ease of access, this must be shown on a map and noise propagation calculations detailed to show how the design criteria is achieved.\r\nb) The plant shall be isolated on adequate proprietary anti-vibration mounts to prevent the structural transmission of vibration and regenerated noise within adjacent or adjoining premises, and these shall be so maintained thereafter.\r\nc) Within 3 months of this decision (following installation of any mechanical services plant which the application refers), a post completion noise assessment shall be submitted for approval to the local planning authority which demonstrates the actual measured rating level of plant operating under normal conditions. All measurements shall be made in accordance with the methodology of BS4142: 2014 (Methods for rating and assessing industrial and commercial sound) and/or its subsequent amendments. \r\nd) Odour control measures shall be fitted to the kitchen ventilation system before the kitchen is first brought into use, with carbon filters as a minimum. The measures put in place shall be retained permanently and shall be kept in full working order and serviced regularly in accordance with the manufacturer's specification.",
    "Condition : 7 - The proposed system shall be maintained at all times in line with the design specification to prevent exhaust nuisance odours.",
    "Condition : 8 - The garden/patio area to the rear shall not be used as a seating area for the hereby approved restaurant at any times."
  ],
